{
  "id": "defender-xdr",
  "name": "Microsoft Defender XDR delegation",
  "version": 3,
  "groupNamePattern": "PIM-{Role}",
  "description": "Permission groups for Defender XDR Unified RBAC. These are workload groups: Defender XDR assigns its RBAC roles directly to the Entra groups (no Entra directory role involved). Each group ships WITH its binding (a PIM-Assignments-Workloads row, connector defender-xdr) carrying the role's permissions and data sources, so the group and its role are imported as one unit: the engine creates the custom role named exactly like the group, keeps its permissions equal to the pack, and assigns it with the listed data sources. Group names follow your own naming pattern. v1 shipped the three operator groups; v2 added the read-only counterparts and the client-scoped response group; v3 adds the permission specs, the Data Operations operator and reader groups, the server-scoped response group and the client- and server-scoped Security Operations and Security Posture operator groups, and moves the Authorization and Settings administrator from L2 to L3 (workload roles are never L2).",
  "knownActionPrefixes": [
    "microsoft.xdr/secops/",
    "microsoft.xdr/securityposture/",
    "microsoft.xdr/configuration/",
    "microsoft.xdr/dataops/"
  ],
